  <id>com.zshadow7x.linuxdoctor</id>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">com.zshadow7x.linuxdoctor.desktop</launchable>
  <name>Linux Doctor</name>
  <summary>Read-only health checks that explain what's wrong and how to fix it</summary>

  <developer id="io.github.zshadow7x">
    <name>7sh1d0w7x</name>
  </developer>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>

  <description>
    <p>
      Linux Doctor runs safe, read-only checks and returns the conclusion instead
      of a wall of raw output: what is wrong, why it matters, and the one command
      to fix it. It remembers the previous run, so every report tells you what is
      new, what got fixed, and what stayed the same.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is deliberately a doctor, not a monitor — it does not stream metrics or
      sit in the background waiting to page you. Run it when something feels off,
      before you file a bug report, or daily from a timer.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Health score (0–100) with an auditable breakdown</li>
      <li>NEW/FIXED diff and a trend line on every run</li>
      <li>One clear next step (▶ START HERE) instead of a wall of graphs</li>
      <li>CLI, web dashboard, and desktop app sharing the exact same checks</li>
      <li>Read-only by construction — fixes are suggestions you run yourself</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Runs on any glibc distribution, including immutable systems such as Fedora
      Silverblue and Bazzite.
    </p>
  </description>

